<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72208" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰδ-έω</span></b> , rarely <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰδάω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			2.734f
		</span></i>: impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾤδεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.455
				</span></i>
			 : aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾤδησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					2.1.7
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				2.2.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				251b
			</span></i> : pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾤδηκα,</span>
			
				Dor.
			
			3pl.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					1.43
				</span></i>
			 ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοιδέω</span>
				:—<i>swell, become swollen,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾤδεε δὲ χρόα πάντα</span>
			<i>he had</i> all his body <i>swollen,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> l. c. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰδῶν τὼ πόδε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					1192
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς πόδας καὶ γαστέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					544.4
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ σφύρ᾽ ᾤδει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxil.
					36
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμβρυα οἰδέοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠδήκαντι κατ᾽ αὐχένα ἶνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
				</span></i>
			 l. c. ; of growing fruits, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπώραν ἐντεταμένην καὶ οἰδῶσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
				</span></i>
			 l. c. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾤδησε . . ὁ τοῦ πτεροῦ καυλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
				</span></i>
			 l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰδεόντων τῶν πρηγμάτων</span> when
			affairs <i>were in a ferment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.76
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				127
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰδεῖ καὶ ὕπουλός ἐστιν [ἡ
				πόλις],</span> metaph. from a boil or abscess, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				518e
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δῆμον οἰδοῦντα καὶ θρασυνόμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Sol.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			 ; also, of inflated style, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰδεῖν ὑπὸ κομπασμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					940
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				26
			</span></i>.</div>
